# --- Language prefixes ---
# /en, /es, /fr and /ar are now REAL paths: the build prerenders a document per
# language for every translated route, each with its own canonical. The old
# rules here rewrote /en/* to /:splat?lang=en, which would now intercept those
# real paths and redirect them away, so they are gone. A prefixed path with no
# translated page falls through to 404.html, which is correct: that page does
# not exist in that language.

# No SPA catch-all. Every real route is written as its own file by the build's
# prerender step, so Cloudflare serves the exact document for a direct hit. A
# blanket "/* /index.html 200" made every wrong URL answer 200 with the app
# shell, which is a soft 404: a crawler asking for /blog-posts-sitemap.xml or
# any stale Wix path got a page instead of an error. With no catch-all,
# unmatched paths fall through to 404.html with a real 404 status.
